---
code: footprint-incoherent
when-fires: a touches() footprint is incoherent. cli/main.rs — TWO emit paths: the SPANNED own-coordinate canary (footprint omits its own effect coordinate), and the SPANLESS malformed-derived-coordinate refusal (the SPANLESS_SITE_PAYLOADS one).
why: 24A §1b / 24E §7: an at-most claim cannot be partial — refuse ⇒ the site walls. The reason is typed: two FootprintIncoherentReason variants, each with its own prose-component, which the `{reason}` hole renders (28L rul-reason-enums-not-sibling-codes).
owns:
  - footprint-incoherent-omits-own-coordinate
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- footprint-incoherent && mise run loom:promote -- footprint-incoherent`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all footprint-incoherent` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork add nginx

-- hork.oracle.sh --
#!/usr/bin/env dorc-sh
# dorc-lang/v0.2
hork__predict() {
   verb=$1; shift
   pkg : sm.dorc.Package = "$1"
   case $verb in
      add) hork --query "$pkg" >/dev/null 2>&1 : sm.dorc.Package:"$pkg"@installed ;;
   esac
}

# The at-most claim names a config file but not the package cell the verb itself establishes, so
# it claims LESS than the site is already known to touch.
hork__disturbs() {
   verb=$1; shift
   case $verb in
      add) printf '%s\n' /etc/hork.conf : disturbs sm.dorc.File ;;
   esac
}

hork__is_converged() {
   hork --query -- "$1"
}

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh -o hork.oracle.sh --risk-faultless-skips
warning[footprint-incoherent]: touches() footprint omits this command's own
effect coordinate (at-least not-within at-most) -- footprint refused, the site
walls
      [ book.sh:2:1
   2 | hork add nginx
     | \____________/
